From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: Render bitmap sprites, Tint output and layers for LMU.

Follow up the Tint-registration fix for Le Mans Ultimate (#777). The
GE-Proton11-7-56 log attached to comment 6000328832 reaches the session but
drops 49,523 bitmap sprite batches, 6,592 effect-image draws and 13,137
layer pops. Registering the Tint object alone does not render its output.

Based on the LMU rendering work by Oleg Makarenko <oleg@makarenk.ooo>
in JacKeTUs/wine:
  99ded70ead6305d9f96aa7c7fb1a80146afbc0d2 (sprite batches)
  05404be1a7e7b1cf3ca0d4e71d6e22562af56bee (bitmap tint / effect images)
  e77300aa837ffea193aa3a2c68f9ccf7638dfa4b (layers)

GE adaptation:
- Keep the current Wine SpriteBatch object and command-list recording.
  Compose sprite and context transforms, convert source pixels to DIPs,
  handle flipped destinations, and support source-rectangle clamping.
- Put tint and sampling bounds on the temporary bitmap brush, not the
  source or render-target bitmap. Multiply RGBA once in the pixel shader;
  honor Tint's ClampOutput. Only evaluate Tint with a bitmap input, rather
  than silently replacing arbitrary effects with their first input.
- Keep the public target unchanged while drawing layers into reusable
  context-owned bitmaps. Freeze content bounds at PushLayer, preserve
  geometry/opacity masks, and composite group opacity at PopLayer.
  Hold resource references, reject overlapping use of an explicit layer,
  unwind incomplete layers at EndDraw, and release the cached buffers
  when the context is destroyed.
- Keep clip ownership in the context. Target isolation from the fork is
  provided by the follow-up d2d1-isolate-target-clip-stacks.patch.
- Add pixel tests for transforms, DPI, tint isolation, mask transforms,
  group opacity, repeated/nested layers, public target identity, and
  unbalanced-layer cleanup.

This is not a general effect-graph renderer or a complete implementation
of all Direct2D compositing/antialiasing modes. Keep existing diagnostics
for unsupported effects/modes. Runtime validation of LMU's HUD is still
required; the accompanying tests have not been run in this environment.

Requires d2d1-register-tint-effect.patch first.

Reference: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/777#issuecomment-6000328832
Sources:
https://github.com/JacKeTUs/wine/commit/99ded70ead6305d9f96aa7c7fb1a80146afbc0d2
https://github.com/JacKeTUs/wine/commit/05404be1a7e7b1cf3ca0d4e71d6e22562af56bee
https://github.com/JacKeTUs/wine/commit/e77300aa837ffea193aa3a2c68f9ccf7638dfa4b
Documentation:
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d2d1_3/nf-d2d1_3-id2d1spritebatch-addsprites
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/direct2d/tint-effect
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/direct2d/direct2d-layers-overview

